+# Cross-Entity Page Data Is Assembled in a Read Model
+
+**Status:** Accepted
+
+## Context
+
+The specialty directory (`REQ-VET-003`) presents the inverse of a relation the model owns. `Vet` holds `Specialty`; the page lists each specialty with the veterinarians holding it. No type carries that inversion today.
+
+[Feature-Package Organization Without a Service Layer](2026-07-31-feature-package-organization.md) records that business rules live in controllers here. `architecture-principles.md` § Pattern Catalog admits no business rule in a web controller.
+
+## Options Considered
+
+1. **Assemble in the controller** — group the repository results inside the handler, as the existing pages do.
+2. **Introduce an application service** — add the project's first service layer between controller and repository.
+3. **Read model from a pure factory** — an immutable type in the feature package, built from the repository results.
+4. **Bidirectional association** — map the inverse side on `Specialty` and read the page from one repository query.
+
+## Decision
+
+Cross-entity page data is assembled in an immutable read model, built by a pure static factory from repository results. The controller reads the repositories, calls the factory, and exposes the result. `SpecialtyDirectory` is the first such type.
+
+Option 4 is rejected because an inverse association on `Specialty` recurses in the serialized veterinarian representation that `Vets` roots. Option 2 is rejected as wider than the page needs, and it reopens a structural decision no single page should settle. Option 1 is rejected because it places the inversion of a domain relation in the web layer, reachable only through MVC infrastructure.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- The inversion is unit-testable without the web layer, so this page does not widen the gap that ADR records.
+- Veterinarians match specialties by identifier. `BaseEntity` defines no value equality, so object-equality matching would hold only inside one persistence context.
+- The read model is per-request state. Nothing new is cached; the veterinarian read still passes through the existing `vets` cache.
+- No service layer appears, so the conflict recorded in that ADR stands unchanged for the existing pages.
+- A later cross-entity page repeats this shape rather than reaching for a service layer.
+
+## Implementation
+
+**Requirements:** REQ-VET-003
+
+## References
+
+- [system-design.md § Contracts](../system-design.md#contracts) — the types realizing this decision
+- [ADR: Feature-Package Organization Without a Service Layer](2026-07-31-feature-package-organization.md) — the layering this decision works within
